==== hyperbricks yaml {!{detail_fragment}} ====
detail_fragment:
  - type: api_fragment_render
  - route: fragments/detail
  - endpoint: https://example.com/catalog
  - method: GET
  - querykeys: [id]
  - response_status:
      required: true
      map: {"404": 404, "503": 503, "409": ignore}
  - inline: '{{if eq .Status 404}}Item not found{{else}}{{.Data.name}}{{end}}'
==== explainer ====
An API fragment can opt into response status mapping on its own route or when embedded in an enclosing page. Enabled defaults to true and priority defaults to zero. Without a proposal the root route's ordinary response status remains the fallback. Mapping preserves diagnostic behavior and dynamically selected errors are no-store.
==== expected json ====
{
  "@type": "<API_FRAGMENT_RENDER>",
  "route": "fragments/detail",
  "endpoint": "https://example.com/catalog",
  "method": "GET",
  "querykeys": ["id"],
  "response_status": {
    "required": true,
    "map": {"404": 404, "503": 503, "409": "ignore"}
  },
  "inline": "{{if eq .Status 404}}Item not found{{else}}{{.Data.name}}{{end}}"
}
